# Project Task Completion & Architecture Report

**Project Name:** Qt User Activity & ETW Network Telemetry System  
**Environment:** Windows 10/11 (x64) | Qt 5.15.2 MSVC2019 64-bit  
**Build Tooling:** Qt Creator, `qmake`, `jom` (MSVC C++17 Compiler)  
**Specification Workflow:** OpenSpec (`spec-driven` schema)  

---

## 1. Executive Summary

This project delivers a high-performance, real-time user activity monitoring and network telemetry logging solution built on C++ and Qt 5. The application enforces administrative privilege elevation at startup via Windows UAC manifest integration, intercepts user input activity (keystrokes, mouse movement, window focus changes), traces kernel and user-mode network events via Event Tracing for Windows (ETW), classifies application protocols (REST API, WebSockets, TLS, DNS, RAW TCP/UDP), and writes structured telemetry logs in append-only **JSON Lines (`.jsonl`)** format.

All planned changes have been implemented, tested, and archived into the canonical specifications tree under `openspec/specs/`.

